  "outfits": {
    "_comment": "Every outfit mesh EquipmentTable can put on Eve (SkeletalMesh on her body skeleton) gets LOD0 CPU access, which the gore slicer needs, and its physics asset gets the ragdoll fix. Vanilla physics assets enable Pelvis-vs-Thigh collision although the capsules overlap by ~10 cm at rest, which blows the ragdoll apart (the flinging), and disable almost everything else, so limbs pass through each other. Here bodies collide across groups and never inside one (some outfits, e.g. CH_P_EVE_09, ship with neighbouring torso bodies colliding, which spins her), except pairs closer than rest_margin cm in the outfit's bind pose (measured per asset by assetkit/outfits.py, for every body, so a jiggle, cape or accessory body resting inside another stops colliding with it). Linear damping 5.0 capped her fall at ~2 m/s (floaty); these bodies are kinematic in gameplay, so this only changes ragdolls. Hair and jiggle bodies keep their other settings. 'only' / 'skip' take mesh-name globs (e.g. only: [\"CH_P_EVE_30*\"]) to trim the mod; every patched mesh is a full copy in the pak and replaces outfit mods for the same mesh.",
    "enabled": true,
    "table": "Local/Data/EquipmentTable",
    "skeleton": "CH_P_EVE_01_Skeleton",
    "only": [],
    "skip": [
      "*Hair*"
    ],
    "cpuaccess_lods": [
      0
    ],
    "groups": {
      "torso": [
        "Bip001-Pelvis",
        "Bip001-Spine",
        "Bip001-Spine1",
        "Bip001-Spine2",
        "Bip001-Neck",
        "Bip001-Head",
        "Bip001-L-Clavicle",
        "Bip001-R-Clavicle"
      ],
      "left_arm": [
